{"seq":27,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T22:33:34.128Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"8aedb331d63de110a58d09005ed9a3634e604ea7249eb5902465feb17010baaf","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, I found five ticket references on Vantorre Group (the parent) across those three places. Two of them probably refer to the same ticket.\n\n| Ticket | What it was | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#PD-4418** | A warehouse supervisor reported that the `Carrier_Dwell_Summary` export dropped timestamps for Dock Door 9 at the 04:00 shift change. | Moss digest 9/15/2025. It says \"the account Nadia runs\", which was Vantorre Group at that time. |\n| **#8841 / #PD-8841** | Missed carrier check-ins and a gate kiosk timeout at the Allentown plant (Gate 4 / Dock Door 12, second shift). | Moss digest 4/27/2026, written as #PD-8841. Moss digest 5/4/2026, still open at handoff. #strategic-pod, 7/1/2026, where Gideon said he closed it. |\n| **#8841 (again)** | Mateo submitted it for the carrier portal. Drivers at the second shift could not select Dock Door 14 on the check-in kiosk at Newark. Gideon escalated it to platform engineering. | Moss digest 9/30/2026. |\n| **INC-4821** | The Hartford gate kiosk outage on 8/3. Gideon attached a screenshot while he was chasing the status-page access issue. | #inc-vtg-hartford, 8/3/2026 |\n| **VT-55120** | Root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage. It holds Carrowmere's gateway route finding and the reconnect log. | #inc-vtg-hartford, Gideon, 10/14/2026 |\n\nThings to check before this goes to Mateo:\n- **#8841 status:** The numbers match, but the status doesn't. The 5/4 digest has it open, Gideon said on 7/1 that he closed it, and the 9/30 digest describes it as newly submitted. The 9/30 digest also places it at Newark, which the other digests tie to Vantorre Mobility. It may be a reused number, a reopened ticket, or a Moss mix-up. Gideon can confirm.\n- **8/3 digest:** It describes the Hartford incident but gives no ticket number.\n- **Excluded:** #4812 (Mobility, digest 3/10/2025) and #PD-4402 (Quillfeather, digest 9/15/2025). I also left out the digests from 7/7/2025, 12/1/2025, 5/3/2026 and the cheat sheet. They mention no ticket numbers.\n- **Coverage:** I read every message in #strategic-pod and #inc-vtg-hartford and all ten Moss digests. I can't see the ticketing system, so this only covers what was written in those places."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
